  "body": "MAINLINE-045 filed. Neither lead is damage tolerant on its own budget. P2: impact dents are narrow (lambda under 0.63), so 015's map leaves gamma alone. But each face carries a fixed 238.7 kN/m on a core that crushes at 0.241 MPa, so a crushed zone over 55 mm (clamped; 27 mm simply supported) grows once deeper than about 0.2-1.5 mm, at BVID. The design 50.8 mm hail crushes about 81 mm and grows on two of three readings; mooring contact at 0.914 m/s crushes through. P2's float margin is 14.6 kg, so no face, core or shield fix fits; venting to 46 percent of the pressure difference (about 2646 kg of air) before hail does. P3: the design hail breaks a tube with probability 1.1-5.3 percent a strike. One lost member multiplies neighbour stress 2.4-3.3 times (linear frame) and drops the film over it to SF 0.84, so the frame cascades. A puncture runs at 1.38 GPa, and a torn bay lands the hull at 23-35 m/s. A tear-stopping film reads SF 0.88-0.98 and 1.5 mm walls read 0.80. A slow leak only lowers the hull: floating neutrally, the difference is M R T/V, plus 1.1 percent from ISA's lapse. Touchdown reaches 0.914 m/s at a 63-66 mm hole, the landing valve is 70-200 mm, and a pressure gauge finds a 0.36 mm hole in an hour. Inspection cannot catch growth, which is immediate. Sixteen NFI rows. The brief names no next job.",
